Chapter: RocRecRoseTree
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 Ported from roc-lang/roc, src/eval/test/eval_recursive_data_tests.zig,
 "inspect: recursive nominal rose tree with children":

     Rose := [Rose(I64, List(Rose))]
     main = Rose.Rose(1, [Rose.Rose(2, []), Rose.Rose(3, [])])

 Roc inspects `Rose(1, [Rose(2, []), Rose(3, [])])`. The constructor is
 spelled `Node` here so it does not share the type's name, and the printer
 spells it back as Roc does. A second line sums the tree, 6.

Section: Types

  Rose =
   | Node (Integer) (List Rose)

Section: Functions

  rose-text : Rose -> Text
  rose-text (r) =
   when r
    is Node (n) (kids) -> "Rose(" & show n & ", [" & join-rose kids 0 & "])"

  join-rose : List Rose, Integer -> Text
  join-rose (kids) (i) =
   if i >= list-length kids then ""
   else if i + 1 == list-length kids then rose-text (list-at kids i)
   else rose-text (list-at kids i) & ", " & join-rose kids (i + 1)

  rose-sum : Rose -> Integer
  rose-sum (r) =
   when r
    is Node (n) (kids) -> n + sum-kids kids 0

  sum-kids : List Rose, Integer -> Integer
  sum-kids (kids) (i) =
   if i >= list-length kids then 0
   else rose-sum (list-at kids i) + sum-kids kids (i + 1)

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing
  opening = act
   let tree = Node 1 [Node 2 [], Node 3 []]
   in act
    print-line-uni (rose-text tree)
    print-line-uni (show (rose-sum tree))
   end
  end
